":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-21T15:43:17Z","updated_at":"2025-04-21T15:43:17Z","body":"Please do not bump PRs without adding additional information","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2818832002/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2874302909","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105476#issuecomment-2874302909","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105476","id":2874302909,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rUmG9","user":{"login":"shiena","id":1295639,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyOTU2Mzk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1295639?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena","html_url":"https://github.com/shiena","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-12T22:02:08Z","updated_at":"2025-05-12T22:02:08Z","body":"@0xafbf \r\nThis patch should fix the build. Clarified the ambiguous `fn`.\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/modules/camera/camera_win.cpp b/modules/camera/camera_win.cpp\r\n--- a/modules/camera/camera_win.cpp\t(revision e777a599ed82278742eb4f8471058cf967e11b8a)\r\n+++ b/modules/camera/camera_win.cpp\t(date 1747086735202)\r\n@@ -43,9 +43,9 @@\r\n #ifndef defer\r\n template<typename Fn>\r\n struct _deferClass {\r\n-\tFn fn;\r\n-\t_deferClass(Fn&& fn): fn(fn){}\r\n-\t~_deferClass() { fn(); }\r\n+\tFn _fn;\r\n+\t_deferClass(Fn&& fn): _fn(fn){}\r\n+\t~_deferClass() { _fn(); }\r\n };\r\n \r\n #define DEFER_CONCAT_INTERNAL(a, b) a##b\r\n\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2874302909/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2892906519","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105476#issuecomment-2892906519","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105476","id":2892906519,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sbkAX","user":{"login":"botero-dev","id":1028756,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjg3NTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1028756?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/botero-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/botero-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/botero-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/botero-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/botero-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/botero-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/botero-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/botero-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/botero-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/botero-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/botero-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-20T04:31:35Z","updated_at":"2025-05-20T04:32:24Z","body":"> @0xafbf This patch should fix the build. Clarified the ambiguous `fn`.\r\n\r\n@shiena Thanks, I ended up removing the macros. Didn't feel like it it matched Godot style too well.\r\n\r\nI updated the code to handle MJPG and YUY2 formats. I also removed the macros and tried to make the code make sense without them.\r\n\r\nThere are still some issues with the code, but at least it compiles well now, and can be tried with this test project:\r\n\r\n\r\n[ui_camera_feed.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20324759/ui_camera_feed.zip)\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2892906519/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2917775169","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105476#issuecomment-2917775169","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105476","id":2917775169,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6t6bdB","user":{"login":"shiena","id":1295639,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyOTU2Mzk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1295639?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena","html_url":"https://github.com/shiena","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-28T22:42:03Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T01:44:23Z","body":"I believe it would be good to update the documentation as follows:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/doc/classes/CameraFeed.xml b/doc/classes/CameraFeed.xml\r\nindex f3e5630971..95ea288a89 100644\r\n--- a/doc/classes/CameraFeed.xml\r\n+++ b/doc/classes/CameraFeed.xml\r\n@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@\r\n \t<description>\r\n \t\tA camera feed gives you access to a single physical camera attached to your device. When enabled, Godot will start capturing frames from the camera which can then be used. See also [CameraServer].\r\n \t\t[b]Note:[/b] Many cameras will return YCbCr images which are split into two textures and need to be combined in a shader. Godot does this automatically for you if you set the environment to show the camera image in the background.\r\n-\t\t[b]Note:[/b] This class is currently only implemented on Linux, macOS, and iOS. On other platforms no [CameraFeed]s will be available. To get a [CameraFeed] on iOS, the camera plugin from [url=https://github.com/godotengine/godot-ios-plugins]godot-ios-plugins[/url] is required.\r\n+\t\t[b]Note:[/b] This class is currently only implemented on Linux, Windows, macOS, and iOS. On other platforms no [CameraFeed]s will be available. To get a [CameraFeed] on iOS, the camera plugin from [url=https://github.com/godotengine/godot-ios-plugins]godot-ios-plugins[/url] is required.\r\n \t</description>\r\n \t<tutorials>\r\n \t</tutorials>\r\ndiff --git a/doc/classes/CameraServer.xml b/doc/classes/CameraServer.xml\r\nindex c9a423efe6..078e2ef958 100644\r\n--- a/doc/classes/CameraServer.xml\r\n+++ b/doc/classes/CameraServer.xml\r\n@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@\r\n \t<description>\r\n \t\tThe [CameraServer] keeps track of different cameras accessible in Godot. These are external cameras such as webcams or the cameras on your phone.\r\n \t\tIt is notably used to provide AR modules with a video feed from the camera.\r\n-\t\t[b]Note:[/b] This class is currently only implemented on Linux, macOS, and iOS. On other platforms no [CameraFeed]s will be available. To get a [CameraFeed] on iOS, the camera plugin from [url=https://github.com/godotengine/godot-ios-plugins]godot-ios-plugins[/url] is required.\r\n+\t\t[b]Note:[/b] This class is currently only implemented on Linux, Windows, macOS, and iOS. On other platforms no [CameraFeed]s will be available. To get a [CameraFeed] on iOS, the camera plugin from [url=https://github.com/godotengine/godot-ios-plugins]godot-ios-plugins[/url] is required.\r\n \t</description>\r\n \t<tutorials>\r\n \t</tutorials>\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2917775169/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3017104905","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/10547